#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:3
msgid "Fields and widgets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:5
msgid "Fields structure the :doc:`models <models_modules_apps>` of a database. If you think of a model as a table or spreadsheet, fields are the columns and records are the individual rows. Fields also define the type of data that is stored within them. The way in which a field's data is presented and formatted on the :abbr:`UI (User Interface)` is controlled by its widget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:10
msgid "With Studio, it is possible to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:12
msgid ":ref:`add new fields <studio/fields/add-new>` to your database. From a technical point of view, there are 15 :ref:`field types <studio/fields/field-types>` in Odoo. However, you can choose from 21 field types in Studio, as some field types are available more than once with a different default widget;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:16
msgid ":ref:`add existing fields, <studio/fields/add-existing>` i.e., fields that already exists on a model, to any view of that model;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:18
msgid ":ref:`modify a field's properties <studio/fields/modify>`; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:19
msgid ":ref:`remove a field from a view <studio/fields/remove>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:21
msgid "Studio fields vs. property fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:23
msgid "Fields created using Studio are saved as columns in your Odoo database. :doc:`Property fields <../essentials/property_fields>`, on the other hand, act as pseudo-fields; they are shared by all records that are linked to the same parent record (e.g., for tasks, the project, or for a product, the product category), but they are not saved as columns in your database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:29
msgid "Adding a :guilabel:`Deadline` field to the form view of a task using Studio makes that field visible in every task in your database. Adding a :guilabel:`Special instructions` property field to a task makes the field visible in all tasks *within the same project* (i.e., its parent) while other projects’ tasks remain unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:37
msgid "Field types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:39
msgid "Fields can be broadly divided into two categories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:41
msgid ":ref:`Simple fields <studio/fields/simple-fields>`, which contain basic values, such as text, numbers, files, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/studio/fields.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`Relational fields <studio/fields/relational-fields>`, which are used to link and display the data from records on another model."
